    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235-a2">

                <pb facs="0511" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg441"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 574.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to Mr.
                            Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 28,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Earl Granville, Her Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs,
                    presents his compliments to Mr. Lowell, the minister of the United States, and
                    in reply to his letter of the 26th instant, begs leave to say that he will have
                    much pleasure in receiving Mr. Lowell at the foreign office at 3 p.m. on Monday,
                    July 2.</p>
            </div>
